  "scope": "Both note and volume callbacks are executable SCT insertion and post-SCT pending-object append, without opaque callback frame premises. Arbitrary Ordinary execution returned results preserve input nonverifiable writes and either preserve verifiable writes or add exactly the two volume marker writes. Whole execution success derives exact capability match, initially absent current overlay entry, and both marker writes, without successful reshape or desired read/poststate premises. Earlier objects/events may remain altered on errors. Rust/tree/store/ownership/proof and full Transfer interfaces remain open. All three executable definitions and nine theorem contracts are unchanged from the failed attempt; successor proof annotations make the two reshape V/NV observations syntactically available at the installed backend alias and discharge a simplified True. Both markers persist after returned volume SCT/pending callback errors in this immutable model. Raw objects/events may remain altered. Successfully loaded immutable trees, actual getter panic, Clone/COW, key/value/event/source projections, tree and reader semantics, block finalization and durability remain explicit interfaces. Failed predecessor full zero credit.",
